1
00:00:06,323 --> 00:00:10,227
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:21,338
If I recall, this case was...

3
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:29,046
This date...

4
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:30,781
Do you remember something?

5
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:32,783
No...

6
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:36,019
July 9th...

7
00:00:36,987 --> 00:00:37,954
That was Eri-san's case.

8
00:00:38,021 --> 00:00:39,589
Mom was a murder suspect.

9
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:44,294
Ah! That disgusting day!

10
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,531
"Tokyo District Court, Komehana Branch"
"July 9th, 2010"

11
00:00:52,235 --> 00:00:54,604
That color's a little too flashy.

12
00:00:54,838 --> 00:00:56,373
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend - Mori Ran"
Really?

13
00:00:56,406 --> 00:00:59,609
Unless it's a deep red, I can't get into
that fighting spirit, now can I?

14
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:01,845
"Lawyer, Ran's Mother
Kisaki Eri"

15
00:01:01,878 --> 00:01:03,547
Today's for revenge.

16
00:01:03,914 --> 00:01:04,948
Revenge?

17
00:01:05,048 --> 00:01:06,716
Revenge on who?

18
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:08,985
Ran...

19
00:01:09,252 --> 00:01:13,457
Whatever happens today,
don't be frightened.

20
00:01:13,957 --> 00:01:14,958
Eh?

21
00:01:17,127 --> 00:01:18,295
"High School Student Detective
Kudo Shin'ichi"

22
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:20,030
Flowers maybe?

23
00:01:20,697 --> 00:01:22,032
She'd like underwear.

24
00:01:22,099 --> 00:01:23,200
Deep red ones.

25
00:01:23,266 --> 00:01:24,401
Eri-san.

26
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:28,205
In foreign countries, it's normal to give
your lover underwear as a present.

27
00:01:28,371 --> 00:01:30,407
This is a present for Ran, isn't it?

28
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:31,708
I'll go with you.

29
00:01:31,775 --> 00:01:34,978
Well, she's not my lover
and this isn't a foreign country.

30
00:01:35,078 --> 00:01:37,614
Then anything's fine.

31
00:01:37,781 --> 00:01:40,317
It's a man's habit to be unclear.

32
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:41,885
Ah, that's right.

33
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:45,222
This is just an ordinary thank-you gift.
Wouldn't food be fine?

34
00:01:45,655 --> 00:01:47,591
That'd be the worst.

35
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:50,794
You don't express any
passion at all with that.

36
00:01:51,428 --> 00:01:53,597
Do that and you'll lose the woman.

37
00:01:54,297 --> 00:01:58,635
Eri-san what was it?
The first present your husband gave you?

38
00:01:59,236 --> 00:02:00,637
This.

39
00:02:02,506 --> 00:02:06,276
Ehh... His choice was
comparatively good for him, wasn't it?

40
00:02:06,676 --> 00:02:08,111
What "choice" did he make?

41
00:02:08,178 --> 00:02:10,647
I'm the one who chose and bought it.

42
00:02:12,015 --> 00:02:14,084
Should have guessed, huh?

43
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:17,354
Sorry! Ah! Thanks for waiting.

44
00:02:17,487 --> 00:02:18,255
Yo.

45
00:02:18,288 --> 00:02:19,623
"Courtroom"

46
00:02:21,858 --> 00:02:25,428
"Tokyo District Court,
Komehana Branch, Courtroom 305"

47
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,966
Dad?

48
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,135
Ala? Sir. What are you doing here?

49
00:02:32,202 --> 00:02:33,803
"Private Detective
Mori Kogoro"

50
00:02:33,904 --> 00:02:36,139
She called for me...

51
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:40,443
Since it's for my precious Reika-chan's trial,
I just had to come.

52
00:02:40,977 --> 00:02:42,913
What on earth are you intending by coming?

53
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:44,614
Hmm...

54
00:02:44,814 --> 00:02:47,150
Your precious Reika-chan, huh...

55
00:02:47,217 --> 00:02:48,485
Hmmf.

56
00:02:48,785 --> 00:02:51,054
You aren't Reiko-chan's
lawyer today, are you?

57
00:02:52,856 --> 00:02:54,624
If you call out that name this time...

58
00:02:54,791 --> 00:02:56,226
...I'll kill you.

59
00:03:07,003 --> 00:03:08,371
Reika-chan!

60
00:03:11,741 --> 00:03:15,045
"Defendant
Saito Reika"

61
00:03:15,178 --> 00:03:16,813
You can do it!

62
00:03:22,552 --> 00:03:28,358
"The defendant in this trial is a hostess
at the snack bar 'Mint Rose,' Saito Reika."

63
00:03:28,725 --> 00:03:31,461
"On May 28th while on her day shift..."

64
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:37,500
"...she was arrested as a suspect in the theft
of 10 million yen from the safe at her work."
($125,000)

65
00:03:37,901 --> 00:03:39,369
"However..."

66
00:03:39,669 --> 00:03:41,671
"She denies the charges..."

67
00:03:41,771 --> 00:03:42,639
"Lawyer
Uchida Shin'ya"

68
00:03:42,706 --> 00:03:45,208
"...and claims she has an alibi
for the time the theft occurred."

69
00:03:45,875 --> 00:03:51,181
"Eri-san is an important
witness proving her alibi..."

70
00:03:51,448 --> 00:03:52,549
"...she says."

71
00:03:52,582 --> 00:03:53,450
"Public Prosecutor
Kamikawa Takumi"

72
00:03:53,516 --> 00:03:56,586
"This Kamikawa is the Tokyo District
Public Prosecutor's Office Ace Prosecutor."

73
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:57,954
"Undefeated Ace
Hanagata Public Prosecutor, Kamikawa Takumi"

74
00:03:58,021 --> 00:03:59,256
He's an incredible Prosecutor.

75
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:00,657
Ah... Mama!'

76
00:04:00,724 --> 00:04:01,658
"Snack Bar Mint Rose's
Itano Masako"

77
00:04:01,725 --> 00:04:04,194
That woman's a lying cat burglar.

78
00:04:04,561 --> 00:04:06,730
You feel like being a supporter
of a woman like that?

79
00:04:07,631 --> 00:04:08,898
Mama.

80
00:04:09,099 --> 00:04:11,735
There's no reason Reika-chan
could be the criminal!

81
00:04:12,602 --> 00:04:17,207
Since I, the great detective whose name reverberates
around the world, Kogoro Mori, have come...

82
00:04:17,307 --> 00:04:20,510
...I will immediately solve
any kind of mystery!

83
00:04:26,416 --> 00:04:27,484
Who's that?

84
00:04:27,784 --> 00:04:29,286
Court is in session.

85
00:04:29,319 --> 00:04:32,055
"2010, Case 1687
Snack Bar "Mint Rose"
Theft (Stolen Cash) Case
3rd Trial"

86
00:04:32,622 --> 00:04:35,225
"The defendant Reika..."

87
00:04:35,292 --> 00:04:36,192
"Witness for the Defense
Kisaki Eri"

88
00:04:36,259 --> 00:04:39,929
"...claims as her alibi that at the time of the crime
she witnessed Eri-san at some other place."

89
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,698
"Therefore..."

90
00:04:41,831 --> 00:04:45,702
"...the essential focus point in proving
the propriety of Reika's crime..."

91
00:04:45,969 --> 00:04:49,806
"...was whether Eri-san actually
was there at that place."

92
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:55,979
When the snack bar, Mint Rose, was robbed of
10 million yen on May 28th at around midnight...

93
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:58,715
...where were you, Kisaki Eri-san?

94
00:04:58,848 --> 00:05:00,250
Objection!

95
00:05:01,117 --> 00:05:04,921
That doesn't prove the defendant's alibi.

96
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:07,390
If the defendant and Kisaki-san
were at the same place...

97
00:05:07,457 --> 00:05:10,093
...the defendant couldn't have
committed that crime. Isn't that right?

98
00:05:10,193 --> 00:05:12,295
Will you withdraw your objection?

99
00:05:13,697 --> 00:05:17,500
Kisaki-san.
Where were you?

100
00:05:18,001 --> 00:05:19,736
In Haidocho...

101
00:05:21,304 --> 00:05:22,539
...at a love hotel.

102
00:05:22,639 --> 00:05:24,207
I saw you.

103
00:05:25,008 --> 00:05:27,277
You were with some oily old man.

104
00:05:28,945 --> 00:05:30,447
Mom was...

105
00:05:30,914 --> 00:05:32,949
She was at a love hotel with a man?

106
00:05:33,149 --> 00:05:35,018
Reika-san must have seen them
around the area.

107
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:38,355
Eri...
Is it true you were at a love hotel?

108
00:05:38,788 --> 00:05:40,657
Tha... that's an affair!

109
00:05:40,824 --> 00:05:42,425
A legitimate betrayal!

110
00:05:42,525 --> 00:05:43,460
Quiet!

111
00:05:43,526 --> 00:05:46,830
Ehh... It's been testified that
the defendant Saito...

112
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:52,669
...on the same day and time, witnessed you
and a man entering the love hotel, "Peach-Peach."

113
00:05:52,736 --> 00:05:54,104
Damn!

114
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,106
A place I don't know about.

115
00:05:56,206 --> 00:05:57,807
Here's the evidence.

116
00:05:57,941 --> 00:06:02,278
I will submit to the Presiding Judge security camera
footage from the entrance of the hotel "Peach-Peach..."

117
00:06:02,412 --> 00:06:03,747
...as evidence.

118
00:06:03,847 --> 00:06:04,914
I see.

119
00:06:04,981 --> 00:06:08,952
That video will be proof the testimonies
of Eri-san and Reika-san match.

120
00:06:08,985 --> 00:06:11,054
I was really surprised.

121
00:06:11,221 --> 00:06:15,625
That some dirty old man and the
beauty lawyer would be going into a love hotel.

122
00:06:15,725 --> 00:06:17,260
What kind of man was it?

123
00:06:17,394 --> 00:06:18,895
Didn't I just tell you?

124
00:06:18,995 --> 00:06:22,332
A dirty. Old. Man.

125
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:26,536
No matter how pretty she may be, a middle-aged
woman just doesn't get her pick of men.

126
00:06:26,603 --> 00:06:28,538
How pitiful.

127
00:06:29,372 --> 00:06:31,608
I was already in the area.

128
00:06:31,908 --> 00:06:35,678
Reika-san, please stop.
Because you're the defendant, you must stay calm.

129
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:37,147
Inexcusable!

130
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,848
Completely inexcusable!

131
00:06:38,915 --> 00:06:42,018
If it were me,
I couldn't stand such a dirty man.

132
00:06:42,685 --> 00:06:44,421
Being held by such a guy...

133
00:06:44,521 --> 00:06:46,322
Ah, it makes me shudder.

134
00:06:47,690 --> 00:06:48,925
You...

135
00:06:49,058 --> 00:06:51,628
Even though you have
a fine and handsome husband...

136
00:06:51,795 --> 00:06:53,396
...to go off with another man...

137
00:06:53,563 --> 00:06:56,065
Did you think I would forgive you for that?!

138
00:06:56,266 --> 00:06:58,535
Think of Ran's feelings!

139
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,938
All of you think so, don't you?

140
00:07:02,605 --> 00:07:06,443
That I'm so much younger
and prettier than that old woman there.

141
00:07:07,977 --> 00:07:09,946
Say, Lawyer Uchida.

142
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:14,451
I went out of my way to testify
for this person's sake.

143
00:07:14,651 --> 00:07:15,885
What's this about?

144
00:07:16,186 --> 00:07:17,420
I'm sorry.

145
00:07:17,487 --> 00:07:19,889
But it's the truth.

146
00:07:20,356 --> 00:07:23,226
You have a glib
and slippery tongue, don't you?

147
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,562
It's just the truth.

148
00:07:25,895 --> 00:07:27,564
Stop it now.

149
00:07:28,898 --> 00:07:30,867
If you talk any further than this...

150
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:34,471
...your own words will take your life.

151
00:07:34,671 --> 00:07:36,372
Hmm...

152
00:07:36,506 --> 00:07:38,274
What you mean is, you'll kill me.

153
00:07:38,441 --> 00:07:39,776
Yes.

154
00:07:40,477 --> 00:07:42,378
Then, as you wish.

155
00:07:44,113 --> 00:07:45,682
Bang!

156
00:08:05,368 --> 00:08:07,437
Reika-chan! Reika-chan.

157
00:08:08,972 --> 00:08:11,140
Someone!
Someone hurry and call for an ambulance!

158
00:08:11,207 --> 00:08:13,142
It's already too late.

159
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:15,645
She's been shot in the head and killed.

160
00:08:21,518 --> 00:08:23,019
Ala.

161
00:08:23,152 --> 00:08:25,288
Is she really dead?

162
00:08:25,855 --> 00:08:27,657
How regrettable.

163
00:08:28,391 --> 00:08:29,626
Eri!

164
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:31,928
Why would you do such a thing...

165
00:08:32,328 --> 00:08:34,697
It couldn't be helped that she died.

166
00:08:34,964 --> 00:08:36,432
What was that!?

167
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,468
A person is dead!

168
00:08:38,568 --> 00:08:39,836
Ala?

169
00:08:40,136 --> 00:08:43,139
You've defied me, too.

170
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:47,410
In that case, just like her,
I'll kill you with my finger gun.

171
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:51,481
Oi. Don't tell me you...

172
00:08:52,048 --> 00:08:54,617
Who will be next?

173
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,122
You?

174
00:09:01,424 --> 00:09:03,059
Or maybe...

175
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,561
...you.

176
00:09:05,094 --> 00:09:06,062
Or maybe...

177
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:09,866
That's an interesting trick, Lawyer Kisaki.

178
00:09:11,367 --> 00:09:14,137
If a person really
can be killed by finger gun...

179
00:09:14,404 --> 00:09:18,207
Then by all means,
please shoot me with your gun.

180
00:09:18,908 --> 00:09:20,710
Ala, are you sure?

181
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:22,178
Shin'ichi, stop it!

182
00:09:22,245 --> 00:09:24,447
Mom, please stop joking around, too.

183
00:09:24,547 --> 00:09:25,782
Eri!

184
00:09:26,215 --> 00:09:27,650
I misjudged you.

185
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:30,353
An adulterer who kills.

186
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:33,523
Were you that lonely without me?

187
00:09:33,623 --> 00:09:34,924
Huh?

188
00:09:35,058 --> 00:09:36,626
What stupidity are you talking about?

189
00:09:36,693 --> 00:09:39,062
Please stop this already.

190
00:09:40,964 --> 00:09:42,799
More importantly than me...

191
00:09:45,034 --> 00:09:48,671
The present we talked about earlier.

192
00:09:49,906 --> 00:09:52,408
What have you picked out in your head?

193
00:09:52,742 --> 00:09:55,678
The expectations hidden in a present
are etched into this fingertip.

194
00:09:57,246 --> 00:09:59,015
If you choose something poorly...

195
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:01,250
...I'll kill you.

196
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:09,225
Sir, I'll leave this old lady to you.

197
00:10:09,425 --> 00:10:11,527
You should kill your wife.

198
00:10:11,628 --> 00:10:13,162
What are you saying?

199
00:10:13,262 --> 00:10:14,430
Eri!

200
00:10:14,564 --> 00:10:19,102
However alluring I may be,
you shouldn't have killed her! Not her!

201
00:10:19,402 --> 00:10:21,104
You there! Calm down!

202
00:10:21,204 --> 00:10:25,041
But this woman killed Reika-chan!

203
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:28,945
And it is the unworthy I...

204
00:10:29,178 --> 00:10:31,648
...the great detective Mori Kogoro,
who is at fault...

205
00:10:35,618 --> 00:10:40,590
Due to me, two women fought over me
and one of those women died.

206
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,291
I...

207
00:10:43,993 --> 00:10:46,629
I can't forgive my allure!

208
00:10:46,696 --> 00:10:48,898
Sergeant!
Take that person there away.

209
00:10:49,465 --> 00:10:51,367
Ah... Wai... wait a minute.

210
00:10:51,434 --> 00:10:52,835
Presiding judge! Presiding judge!

211
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,837
Dad!

212
00:10:55,638 --> 00:10:58,408
I'm disappointed, Lawyer Kisaki.

213
00:10:58,941 --> 00:11:01,911
I can't stand that attitude of yours.

214
00:11:05,181 --> 00:11:09,052
Presiding judge. Please have
Lawyer Kisaki arrested right away.

215
00:11:09,118 --> 00:11:14,257
She is the prime suspect in
the murder of Saito Reika-san.

216
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,325
Shin'ichi?

217
00:11:28,705 --> 00:11:30,840
Very well.
Thank you very much.

218
00:11:30,907 --> 00:11:32,208
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Sato Miwako"

219
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:33,242
Detective Sato.

220
00:11:33,309 --> 00:11:34,343
Kudo-kun.

221
00:11:34,377 --> 00:11:35,478
The corpse...?

222
00:11:35,545 --> 00:11:38,548
One shot, bang, to the head.
An instant death.

223
00:11:38,748 --> 00:11:39,882
Sato-san.

224
00:11:40,016 --> 00:11:41,584
Takagi-kun, how'd it go?

225
00:11:41,684 --> 00:11:43,286
Wherever I look, I can't find the weapon.

226
00:11:43,319 --> 00:11:44,454
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Takagi Wataru"

227
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,556
It clearly looks like a bullet wound...

228
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:50,259
...but it's impossible to have
brought a gun into the courtroom.

229
00:11:50,426 --> 00:11:52,628
Since just the one shot was fired...

230
00:11:52,762 --> 00:11:57,934
...it's possible a metal tube with a detonator could
function to have a bullet shot out of it, right?

231
00:11:58,234 --> 00:12:02,138
So we should first locate
who used the weapon.

232
00:12:02,405 --> 00:12:06,042
Prosecutor Kamikawa,
what did you notice at the crime scene...

233
00:12:06,209 --> 00:12:08,745
The bizarre behavior of Lawyer Kisaki.

234
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:12,715
She herself said she had killed her
and gave what could be called a confession.

235
00:12:12,849 --> 00:12:17,720
The one who killed Saito Reika-san was you,
Lawyer Kisaki, wasn't it?

236
00:12:18,921 --> 00:12:20,289
No.

237
00:12:20,556 --> 00:12:21,424
You're wrong.

238
00:12:21,457 --> 00:12:23,760
Are you retracting your earlier statements?

239
00:12:24,694 --> 00:12:26,696
Common sense alone
should tell you, shouldn't it?

240
00:12:27,096 --> 00:12:31,033
Don't tell me you actually believe a person
can be killed with a finger gun, do you?

241
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,836
Then, all that earlier was a joke, huh?

242
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:35,838
Obviously.

243
00:12:36,239 --> 00:12:40,042
Or do you intend to
write up in your report...

244
00:12:40,143 --> 00:12:42,011
"Deadly weapon,
a human's second finger (index finger)"

245
00:12:42,044 --> 00:12:45,515
..."Deadly weapon,
a human's second finger (index finger)"?

246
00:12:46,349 --> 00:12:48,451
What a laugh.

247
00:12:50,386 --> 00:12:51,921
Say, Shin'ichi.

248
00:12:53,156 --> 00:12:54,524
Mom is...

249
00:12:55,057 --> 00:12:57,226
Mom isn't the criminal, right?

250
00:12:58,761 --> 00:13:00,096
Shin'ichi?

251
00:13:00,229 --> 00:13:03,232
That woman could have done it.

252
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:04,700
Eh?

253
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:10,106
Reika and your mother had
a huge fight over Kogoro-chan.

254
00:13:10,239 --> 00:13:12,108
It was pandemonium.
Pandemonium.

255
00:13:12,141 --> 00:13:13,476
Ow, ow, ow!

256
00:13:14,243 --> 00:13:15,478
"Reika!"

257
00:13:17,113 --> 00:13:20,082
"Reika!"

258
00:13:21,184 --> 00:13:25,822
If this story about Lawyer Kisaki
and Reika-san is true...

259
00:13:25,955 --> 00:13:27,623
...then she would have a motive.

260
00:13:27,690 --> 00:13:29,625
They were fighting over a man.

261
00:13:29,792 --> 00:13:31,627
They clashed at a hotel, didn't they?

262
00:13:31,761 --> 00:13:33,896
Reika and that lawyer.

263
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:36,399
No matter how you look at it, it's strange.

264
00:13:36,866 --> 00:13:38,601
Say, Shin'ichi...

265
00:13:41,137 --> 00:13:42,772
Mom was talking about it.

266
00:13:43,272 --> 00:13:44,774
That she was going...

267
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:47,276
...to take revenge today.

268
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:49,278
Ran, that was...

269
00:13:49,545 --> 00:13:51,514
But, there's no way
Mom could be the criminal.

270
00:13:51,814 --> 00:13:54,283
It's impossible that Mom
could be the criminal.

271
00:13:57,386 --> 00:13:58,588
Prosecutor Kamikawa...

272
00:13:58,688 --> 00:14:02,124
...about that security camera video from the
love hotel that was at issue during the trial.

273
00:14:02,358 --> 00:14:03,926
Is there anything shown on that?

274
00:14:04,026 --> 00:14:05,061
On the video?

275
00:14:05,127 --> 00:14:07,530
It's possible something will come from it.

276
00:14:07,730 --> 00:14:09,165
Something that the Lawyer Kisaki...

277
00:14:09,298 --> 00:14:11,167
...is trying to hide.

278
00:14:14,036 --> 00:14:17,540
At the same time Reika-san
was outside of this love hotel...

279
00:14:17,707 --> 00:14:19,475
...she saw Kisaki-san with a man, right?

280
00:14:19,575 --> 00:14:22,478
Yeah. That's why Reika-san
doesn't show up in the video.

281
00:14:22,578 --> 00:14:25,248
Lawyer Uchida, how did you come
into possession of this video?

282
00:14:25,448 --> 00:14:28,217
After hearing her testimony,
I hurriedly looked for it.

283
00:14:28,384 --> 00:14:30,820
It was a big help that the video
was still around.

284
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,289
Speaking of which...

285
00:14:33,389 --> 00:14:36,859
...before she was killed, those reckless remarks
Reika-san spat out and her attitude...

286
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,895
Were those under your directions,
Lawyer Uchida?

287
00:14:39,028 --> 00:14:40,463
Nothing of the sort!

288
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:43,833
All it would do is make a bad impression
on the judge, wouldn't it?

289
00:14:44,066 --> 00:14:47,637
I can't even begin to guess
what it was that got her so upset.

290
00:14:56,312 --> 00:15:01,517
It seems you were at the love hotel at the
time of the crime, just as Saito Reika testified.

291
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,886
I didn't testify I wasn't, did I?

292
00:15:04,053 --> 00:15:08,024
With this, Reika-san's alibi
has been proven.

293
00:15:08,557 --> 00:15:10,826
We can say she was innocent.

294
00:15:21,137 --> 00:15:22,271
Eri-san...

295
00:15:22,638 --> 00:15:25,408
Who is this man that you're with?

296
00:15:27,376 --> 00:15:29,078
You won't answer?

297
00:15:37,386 --> 00:15:39,322
"Eri-san squatted."

298
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:42,558
"Finger gun."

299
00:15:43,726 --> 00:15:45,461
"Love hotel."

300
00:15:45,761 --> 00:15:46,829
"Revenge."

301
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:48,030
"Today's for revenge."

302
00:15:48,064 --> 00:15:50,166
"A quarrel with grabbing."

303
00:15:51,467 --> 00:15:52,935
"Reckless remarks."

304
00:15:57,106 --> 00:15:59,475
The pieces have been gathered.

305
00:16:00,476 --> 00:16:01,844
All that's left...

306
00:16:05,181 --> 00:16:07,516
...is to prove the truth.

307
00:16:08,851 --> 00:16:10,219
Eri-san.

308
00:16:10,786 --> 00:16:15,024
You didn't want that video
earlier to be seen, did you?

309
00:16:15,157 --> 00:16:17,326
That's why you killed Reika-san.

310
00:16:17,626 --> 00:16:19,095
Shin'ichi?

311
00:16:19,295 --> 00:16:20,296
Hey, what are you saying?

312
00:16:20,363 --> 00:16:21,697
Ran.

313
00:16:21,964 --> 00:16:23,699
By my deduction...

314
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,868
...Eri-san is the criminal.

315
00:16:26,702 --> 00:16:32,108
The Lawyer Kisaki had to kill
Saito Reika-san in this courtroom.

316
00:16:32,375 --> 00:16:33,909
Her reason...

317
00:16:34,110 --> 00:16:38,447
...was that this video would then
no longer be disclosed to the court.

318
00:16:39,949 --> 00:16:41,984
What was on this video...

319
00:16:42,318 --> 00:16:45,888
...was certain evidence of your adultery.

320
00:16:46,555 --> 00:16:48,057
By allowing this to run...

321
00:16:48,324 --> 00:16:50,493
...your divorce would
have been made definite.

322
00:16:52,128 --> 00:16:53,996
You say that so dryly.

323
00:16:54,563 --> 00:16:57,566
I could divorce
such a man as him at any time.

324
00:16:57,633 --> 00:16:59,435
Still Lawyer Kisaki...

325
00:16:59,502 --> 00:17:02,638
...you were quarreling
with Reika-san over Kogoro.

326
00:17:02,738 --> 00:17:04,774
That was surely a woman's jealousy.

327
00:17:05,241 --> 00:17:06,575
It was just pride.

328
00:17:06,876 --> 00:17:08,878
Shape up, Shin'ichi!

329
00:17:09,879 --> 00:17:11,080
Ran...

330
00:17:11,914 --> 00:17:14,016
Mom couldn't kill a person.

331
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,918
Shin'ichi, you know that, don't you!

332
00:17:16,052 --> 00:17:17,920
Because Mom is honest...

333
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:23,359
...and always right and a perfect mother.

334
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,194
Ran.

335
00:17:25,694 --> 00:17:27,029
What is this?

336
00:17:28,898 --> 00:17:30,933
Does the perfect person...

337
00:17:31,534 --> 00:17:34,270
...go to a love hotel with a suspicious man?

338
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:38,841
Eh? That's...

339
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:40,843
Ran-san.

340
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:46,816
Hasn't it been a burden for Lawyer Kisaki?
It's the height of her evaluation period.

341
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:48,717
Lies...

342
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,619
I won't believe it.

343
00:17:50,886 --> 00:17:52,488
I absolutely won't believe it.

344
00:17:52,555 --> 00:17:54,457
My daughter's right.

345
00:17:56,192 --> 00:17:58,260
I am not the criminal.

346
00:17:59,895 --> 00:18:05,034
The point is, making a fuss over
a video is a weak foundation.

347
00:18:05,201 --> 00:18:07,036
It's well-founded.

348
00:18:07,837 --> 00:18:10,172
"Reika-chan! Reika-chan!"

349
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:11,740
When you fell down...

350
00:18:11,907 --> 00:18:15,344
...it was to pick up the mortal weapon
you had dropped, wasn't it?

351
00:18:15,811 --> 00:18:21,117
And then, you picked a quarrel with
everyone so you could cheat your movements.

352
00:18:21,417 --> 00:18:22,985
Where's your evidence?

353
00:18:25,054 --> 00:18:26,922
You must have evidence, don't you?

354
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:30,926
After the incident, you were
immediately placed under guard.

355
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,394
Therefore...

356
00:18:32,761 --> 00:18:34,864
...you should still be
concealing the weapon.

357
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,866
Do a body search.

358
00:18:49,712 --> 00:18:51,380
Excuse me.

359
00:18:57,987 --> 00:19:01,757
I couldn't find a deadly weapon.

360
00:19:01,857 --> 00:19:03,526
Eh? Why?

361
00:19:03,592 --> 00:19:06,428
Is Lawyer Kisaki the criminal... or not?

362
00:19:06,695 --> 00:19:07,997
Well...

363
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:12,635
It's impossible the excellent Lawyer Kisaki not
to have someplace she could hide it quickly.

364
00:19:12,868 --> 00:19:14,203
In that case...

365
00:19:14,637 --> 00:19:16,906
...the deadly weapon could only be there.

366
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:21,410
Please untie your hair, Lawyer Kisaki.

367
00:19:21,977 --> 00:19:24,113
What is it? Can't you do it?

368
00:19:42,164 --> 00:19:44,567
The deadly weapon.
I've found the deadly weapon.

369
00:19:45,034 --> 00:19:47,503
There's no doubt that she's the criminal.

370
00:19:48,637 --> 00:19:51,073
Is that really the mortal weapon?

371
00:19:51,307 --> 00:19:52,341
Here, take a good look.

372
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,677
In here's the equipment to fire a bullet.

373
00:20:05,487 --> 00:20:08,624
Seems to be an ordinary tube of lipstick.

374
00:20:09,024 --> 00:20:12,027
At last you've revealed you're at fault,
haven't you, Prosecutor Kamikawa.

375
00:20:13,195 --> 00:20:15,431
It was shown in the
criminal investigation report...

376
00:20:15,564 --> 00:20:19,635
...that the mortal weapon was
a metal tube of some sort.

377
00:20:19,835 --> 00:20:22,438
Not knowing either its features
nor its dimensions...

378
00:20:22,538 --> 00:20:26,609
...there wasn't anyone but the criminal who would
conclude the deadly weapon was this lipstick.

379
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:31,847
And...
The real mortal weapon is in this.

380
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:44,693
Prosecutor Kamikawa, don't you think
it's been shown at last with this?

381
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:46,495
What's that?

382
00:20:46,629 --> 00:20:49,865
The riddle of the lie from
the weapon's victim.

383
00:20:50,065 --> 00:20:51,500
In other words...

384
00:20:52,067 --> 00:20:57,239
...what remains in this court is just
the guy with the one and only truth.

385
00:21:01,477 --> 00:21:04,880
You made a gun from the same
tube of lipstick that Eri-san had...

386
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:08,550
...and then smuggled it into the court.

387
00:21:08,717 --> 00:21:12,688
And then you waited for a chance
when Reika-san was making a fuss...

388
00:21:12,821 --> 00:21:15,357
...to aim and fire the gun...

389
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:32,541
You then rolled the gun to
the witness stand where Eri-san was.

390
00:21:33,108 --> 00:21:37,479
When it rolled up to me,
I thought it was my lipstick.

391
00:21:37,746 --> 00:21:40,749
But when I picked it up, I noticed it was
strangely hot and so then I understood.

392
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:43,185
That if my fingerprints were left on it...

393
00:21:43,352 --> 00:21:45,954
...I would be tagged as the criminal.

394
00:21:46,188 --> 00:21:52,061
So I indeed acted suspiciously
and gave a signal to Shin'ichi-kun.

395
00:21:55,097 --> 00:21:57,800
I deduced that this line was,
"Use your head."

396
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:01,170
"What present have you
picked out in your head?"

397
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,638
The "present" was lipstick.

398
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,740
"Fingertip" meant fingerprint.

399
00:22:05,274 --> 00:22:08,444
By "If you choose something poorly,"
she meant deadly weapon.

400
00:22:08,610 --> 00:22:10,979
"If you choose something poorly..."

401
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:15,684
From those hints,
I understood Eri-san's message.

402
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:21,290
That when the deadly weapon wasn't found,
the criminal would surely give themselves away.

403
00:22:21,523 --> 00:22:24,026
So at the moment
that man was making a fuss...

404
00:22:24,326 --> 00:22:27,096
...I turned the mortal weapon
over to Shin'ichi-kun...

405
00:22:27,196 --> 00:22:32,167
And I hid the weapon in this video case
for safe keeping.

406
00:22:33,168 --> 00:22:34,470
Geez...

407
00:22:34,703 --> 00:22:37,072
The two of you had me worried.

408
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:41,877
Kudo-kun.

409
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:47,216
You're under the impression the thing you saw
was the mortal weapon and that I dropped it.

410
00:22:47,349 --> 00:22:49,118
Is there any evidence of that?

411
00:22:49,218 --> 00:22:55,224
Then, how do you explain the mystery
of the lie Reika-san told?

412
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:57,226
Lie?

413
00:22:57,326 --> 00:23:01,463
Before she was killed,
Reika-san told one big, fat lie.

414
00:23:01,897 --> 00:23:03,766
The case of her alibi.

415
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:09,772
Reika-san wasn't in front of the
love hotel at the time of the crime.

416
00:23:10,072 --> 00:23:12,474
She was stealing the money
from the snack bar.

417
00:23:12,574 --> 00:23:14,376
How can you say such a thing?!

418
00:23:14,977 --> 00:23:16,378
Because...

419
00:23:16,545 --> 00:23:18,347
Right, Eri-san?

420
00:23:19,114 --> 00:23:20,716
Right?

421
00:23:20,783 --> 00:23:23,619
She was saying
some strange things, wasn't she?

422
00:23:24,052 --> 00:23:25,621
Strange things?

423
00:23:26,255 --> 00:23:27,389
Yes.

424
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:30,826
That I was together with
a little, dirty old man.

425
00:23:30,993 --> 00:23:32,327
I don't get it.

426
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:35,631
What is this lie the victim was talking about?

427
00:23:36,432 --> 00:23:38,267
Can't be helped.

428
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,903
Geez, then shouldn't you just
call for that little, dirty old man?

429
00:23:41,236 --> 00:23:42,905
If you would please!

430
00:23:49,077 --> 00:23:51,213
Tah-dah!

431
00:23:51,713 --> 00:23:53,615
Thanks for waiting, Ladies and Gentlemen!

432
00:23:54,016 --> 00:23:57,453
I am the famous
and great detective, Mori Kogoro!

433
00:23:57,586 --> 00:23:59,388
We weren't particularly waiting...

434
00:23:59,488 --> 00:24:02,124
And that "fame" doesn't seem
to be selling all that much.

435
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:03,625
What's that?

436
00:24:03,826 --> 00:24:06,762
Saying I'm not popular!
That's just foolishness!

437
00:24:06,795 --> 00:24:07,729
Well then...

438
00:24:07,796 --> 00:24:10,732
...shall we look at the false evidence?

439
00:24:14,336 --> 00:24:15,504
Ala?

440
00:24:15,938 --> 00:24:18,106
Isn't that Kogoro-chan?

441
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,075
Dad?!

442
00:24:20,442 --> 00:24:24,346
The man you went to a love hotel with...
was Dad?!

443
00:24:24,847 --> 00:24:28,417
Ah! I remember!

444
00:24:28,784 --> 00:24:32,688
That was the time Reika-san dumped me,
so I got drunk and called Eri.

445
00:24:32,988 --> 00:24:35,224
Dad! You're the worst!

446
00:24:35,424 --> 00:24:40,128
The man Eri-san was with
was Mori Kogoro.

447
00:24:42,297 --> 00:24:44,333
Strange, isn't it?

448
00:24:44,666 --> 00:24:48,103
Kogoro was a regular customer at her bar.

449
00:24:48,537 --> 00:24:54,409
If she really had witnessed us,
she should have just said so.

450
00:24:55,177 --> 00:24:59,381
"I saw Kisaki and Mori
going into a love hotel."

451
00:25:00,816 --> 00:25:02,084
In other words...

452
00:25:02,184 --> 00:25:08,156
...you could say that Reika-san really
didn't see Eri-san or Kogoro-san.

453
00:25:09,324 --> 00:25:14,596
Then how could Reika-san,
who wasn't at this place, know about it?

454
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:18,867
Reika-san actually didn't see Eri-san.

455
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:23,672
She learned about this video
from someone else.

456
00:25:24,373 --> 00:25:25,874
Prosecutor Kamikawa.

457
00:25:26,208 --> 00:25:27,876
You were in charge of...

458
00:25:28,043 --> 00:25:32,114
...that tax evasion case against the love hotel
"Peach-Peach Group" until recently, weren't you?

459
00:25:32,281 --> 00:25:33,315
"In Charge of the Peach-Peach Group's
Tax Evasion Case"

460
00:25:33,415 --> 00:25:37,653
The only one who could have given her the
information that was on this video in advance...

461
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:41,957
...was you, Prosecutor Kamikawa.

462
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:51,667
Was the motive tangled up in love and money?

463
00:25:52,768 --> 00:25:57,439
Weren't you receiving
unlawful money from Reika-san?

464
00:25:58,473 --> 00:26:00,576
The Elite Public Prosecutor.

465
00:26:05,314 --> 00:26:06,682
She...

466
00:26:07,583 --> 00:26:09,585
She was completely evil!

467
00:26:11,386 --> 00:26:13,755
She was totally mad about me.

468
00:26:14,156 --> 00:26:17,893
I was doing well what with a lover,
money coming in, and a promotion at work.

469
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:20,629
My life was just a lump of good fortune.

470
00:26:21,129 --> 00:26:22,331
Then...

471
00:26:23,031 --> 00:26:24,533
"Don't mess around with me!"

472
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:28,437
As soon as she was arrested,
she had her hand out in return.

473
00:26:28,637 --> 00:26:31,540
Unless I got her out of prison immediately
for stealing that 10 million yen for my sake...

474
00:26:31,740 --> 00:26:37,145
...she said she would reveal everything
that had happened between us before.

475
00:26:38,080 --> 00:26:41,984
The biggest blunder of my life was in
getting caught up with that ill-natured woman.

476
00:26:42,217 --> 00:26:44,386
For the sake of a special man like me...

477
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:46,221
...she should be expected to die!

478
00:26:46,254 --> 00:26:48,056
What's so special about you?!

479
00:26:49,825 --> 00:26:54,496
You're no different than
any other criminal anywhere.

480
00:26:56,531 --> 00:27:00,636
You're just a tiny, stupid man.

481
00:27:06,408 --> 00:27:08,710
Prosecutor Kamikawa! No...

482
00:27:09,444 --> 00:27:10,846
Kamikawa Takumi.

483
00:27:11,013 --> 00:27:14,016
You are under arrest for suspicion
in the murder of Saito Reika.

484
00:27:25,761 --> 00:27:28,497
Ran, I'm sorry.

485
00:27:28,964 --> 00:27:30,632
You must have been frightened.

486
00:27:32,601 --> 00:27:34,069
Yeah.

487
00:27:35,771 --> 00:27:37,406
But, it's okay.

488
00:27:38,306 --> 00:27:40,475
I trusted in Mom, after all.

489
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:47,315
Say, your father...

490
00:27:47,382 --> 00:27:49,951
When we went into that hotel, he passed out
and went to sleep right away.

491
00:27:50,018 --> 00:27:53,355
Huh? Ah... Dad's the worst!

492
00:27:53,722 --> 00:27:56,291
Choose your man carefully, okay?

493
00:27:57,025 --> 00:27:59,461
Don't run away, Sir.

494
00:27:59,961 --> 00:28:01,730
Oi, boy detective.

495
00:28:02,030 --> 00:28:04,533
Choose your wife carefully, okay?

496
00:28:06,501 --> 00:28:07,569
Farewell!

497
00:28:07,636 --> 00:28:13,275
In that case, the only thing that's clear
is that Dad's the worst, isn't it?

498
00:28:13,375 --> 00:28:15,210
Wha... what are you doing?

499
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:19,181
It was only because of my play-acting
that we were able to settle that case.

500
00:28:19,347 --> 00:28:21,450
If so, then it's the deadly weapon...

501
00:28:22,951 --> 00:28:24,619
"Lipstick"

502
00:28:39,701 --> 00:28:42,804
Oi! What case is it this time?

503
00:28:48,710 --> 00:28:51,480
Whaa! Beautiful!

504
00:28:51,513 --> 00:28:52,547
What's this?

505
00:28:52,647 --> 00:28:54,916
If I recall, this dress is...

506
00:28:55,083 --> 00:28:56,418
My dress!

507
00:28:56,485 --> 00:28:58,320
You aren't a wife yet!

508
00:28:58,420 --> 00:28:59,888
